snmp- SNMP, or Simple Network Management Protocol, is a widely used internet standard protocol for monitoring and managing network devices
so i used the hint "**Use a tool like snmp-check or snmp-walk to enumerate SNMP.**"
so lets find those tools syntax and how to use them:

snmp-check : 
Scan the target host (192.168.1.2) using the public SNMP community string (-c public):
syntax: snmp-check 192.168.1.2 -c public

snmp-walk:
An SNMP walk is a process of sequentially retrieving all the available information from a network device using SNMP GETNEXT requests. It's a way to gather a large amount of data, especially when the specific OIDs (Object Identifiers) you're looking for aren't known beforehand. 
syntax: snmpwalk -v1 -c public 192.168.8.1

